{
  "_README": [
    "MCP configuration template for HORIZUN-PBI-MCP (client: Claude Code).",
    "Do NOT use as-is: the <...> placeholders must be replaced with ABSOLUTE paths.",
    "",
    "Recommended way (resolves paths on your machine automatically):",
    "    python scripts/make_mcp_config.py --client claude-code --write",
    "",
    "Manual way: copy this file as .mcp.json and replace:",
    "    <PYTHON_EXE>   path to the interpreter, e.g. C:/Python313/python.exe",
    "                   (if using a venv, point to THAT venv's python.exe)",
    "    <PROJECT_ROOT> path to this folder, e.g. C:/dev/horizun-pbi-mcp",
    "",
    "If you installed the package (pip install horizun-pbi-mcp), it's simpler:",
    "    \"command\": \"horizun-pbi-mcp\", \"args\": []",
    "",
    "On Windows use forward slashes (/) inside the JSON, or escape backslashes",
    "(\\). Don't leave paths from another machine.",
    "",
    "Environment variables: the current prefix is HORIZUN_PBI_MCP_*. The old",
    "PBI_MCP_* variables are still accepted for compatibility, but the new",
    "ones take priority.",
    "",
    "Other clients (Claude Desktop, Codex, generic stdio): see docs/INSTALL.md",
    "",
    "This _README key is documentation only; MCP clients ignore it."
  ],
  "mcpServers": {
    "horizun-pbi-mcp": {
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "<PYTHON_EXE>",
      "args": [
        "<PROJECT_ROOT>/src/server.py"
      ],
      "env": {
        "HORIZUN_PBI_MCP_LOG_LEVEL": "INFO"
      }
    }
  }
}